{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund NHS fast-track pathway for all hyper-aggressive rare cancers",
        "additional_details": "I am starting this petition in memory of my daughter, Jemma, who died after Small Cell Neuroendocrine Cervical Cancer\u2014a disease often called a \"virulent beast\"\u2014progressed with devastating speed. Current 31- or 62-day waits via standard pathways risk allowing patients with rare, fast-doubling malignancies to deteriorate. These cancers must be treated as medical emergencies requiring urgent inpatient care\u2014sparing patients exhausting daily travel\u2014with 24/7 diagnostic reviews, including weekends.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to fund an emergency NHS fast-track pathway for all hyper-aggressive, virulent rare cancers, providing immediate diagnostic review and urgent inpatient treatment for fast-doubling malignancies such as Small Cell Neuroendocrine cancers.",
